<div id="content-body">
    <h1>Company History</h1>
    <hr />
    <div>
        <h1>Early Years 1997-2003</h1>
        <br />
        <p>Davao Unified Corporation (DUC) was incorporated through the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) inDavao City, Philippines in March of 1997.  It opened its doors to its very first customers in June of 1997 as a wholesaler of paper products manufactured by one of its founding incorporators.</p>
<p>DUC operated from its very first warehouse and office in Sta. Ana corner Alvarez Street in Davao City.  The operations back then were simple.  Buy paper in bulk from the founder&#8217;s factory in the island of Luzon, hire a couple of sales persons (Tony Go-Aco, Robert Delima and Marlon Panes are among the first ones) to ply the wholesale routes in Southern Mindanao, and sell everything cheap and mostly through credit terms!   Due to strong competitive advantages in paper products brought about by good factory support, DUC was able to make a name for itself in the wholesale trade as a supplier of quality paper products at the best prices in Southern Mindanao, if not the whole of Mindanao.</p>
<p>However, margins for paper products are not very good.  In the succeeding year &#8212; DUC, a company that only distributed paper, soon expanded its product line to include other School and Office Supplies (SOS) products to improve margins and enhance it strategic position among clients.  These included things such as notebooks, writing instruments, filing supplies and other non-paper products that are used everyday by students and teachers of all levels.  Still, the primary business of DUC was to sell these SOS products through the wholesale trade at the best prices.</p>
<p>In 2001, four successful years after its founding, DUC opened its first retail store in front of its warehouse in Sta. Ana cornerAlvarez Street.  The retail store served two functions:  First, to help DUC become more visible as the store would carry a huge store signage that should be able to advertise the company quite visibly to the general public.  In addition, the store provided a more physical interaction between the company, its customers and the physical goods.  For the first time, the company can actually let its customers see and feel the products that they are buying.  To set the DUC Retail Store apart, the company decided that the store will have to be different from traditional wholesale stores in the SOS industry.  As it is, most wholesale stores enclose most of their goods in glass cases and shelves and required customers to always seek assistance from store staff.  This model was the tried and tested &#8212; and old and slow.  Taking a page from the supermarkets, the company made the store in DIY (Do-It-Yourself) fashion.</p>
<p>Second, the store functioned as a venue for the company to sell products in cash!  This was a big deal, since before the store opened, virtually all sales were made via credit terms.  The cash generated from the store significantly helped the company in  its initial years to generate the proper cash flow to support growth in the coming years.</p>
<p>Furthermore, to support this growing operation, a freelance programmer by the name of Franklin Raz was hired in 1998 to implement the first working software of DUC to manage the wholesale selling and credit and collection functions.  From initial development, continuous development and retirement, the first software of DUC lasted 8 years from 1998 until 2006.</p>
<p>Infomark POS software was installed in 2001 at the DUC Retail Store to automate cashiering functions.  It was retired in 2005.</p>
<p>In early 2003, DUC became the co-exclusive distributor (with GH Office Depot) in Southern Mindanao for AMSPEC products, most known as the original maker of Mongol pencils and Crayola crayons in thePhilippines.  DUC also distributed newsprint papers for PICOP industries for the whole of Mindanao.</p>
<h1></h1>
<h1>Next Phase</h1>
<p>In 2003, a change of management took place.  The following timeline summarizes the milestones that transpired since then:</p>
<h2></h2>
<h2>2003</h2>
<p>- Management Change.</p>
<p>- Initiated change of software systems to cope with growing demands and future proof essential technologies vital to the company.</p>
<h2></h2>
<h2>2004</h2>
<p>- Simultaneously opened the first two stores of The Paper Tree: one near the University of Mindanao in Matina (UM Matina Drive) and another store in Matina Aplaya in McArthur Highwayunder the pedestrian overpass.</p>
<p>- Opened a total of 5 stores in 6 months, with great thanks to Engineer Alviar.</p>
<p>1.) UM Matina Drive</p>
<p>2.) Matina Aplaya in McArthur Highway</p>
<p>3.) San Pedro College</p>
<p>4.) CM Recto (Former Giomiche Educational Supplies)</p>
<p>5.) UM Bolton(Former Visayan Educational Supplies)</p>
<p>- New POS deployed developed by Hubport</p>
<p>- Launched &#8220;Hi&#8221; Ball Pen in the market.</p>
<h2><a href="http://thepapertreeacademy.files.wordpress.com/2012/01/3-awards.jpg"><img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-783" title="3 Awards" src="http://thepapertreeacademy.files.wordpress.com/2012/01/3-awards.jpg?w=500" alt=""   /></a></h2>
<h2></h2>
<h2>2005</h2>
<p>- The Paper Tree in Davao Doctors was opened</p>
<p>- Internal IT Department was established</p>
<p>- Casa De Davao Ladies&#8217; Dormitory in the Paper Tree Bolton complex was opened.</p>
<h2></h2>
<h2>2006</h2>
<p>- Launched new ERP Software which is fully developed in-house.</p>
<p>- Opened The Paper Tree Arcade at The Paper Tree Bolton complex.</p>
<p>- Replaced Hubport POS system with in-house developed system.</p>
<p>- Launched HR Toolkit internally.  This software automated the payroll and HR functions.  ATM payment of regular employees now made through this software.</p>
<h2></h2>
<h2>2007</h2>
<p>- Opened Fuji Printing for printing and producing SOS products such as educational workbooks, formal theme books, columnar notebooks, filing supplies such as magazine filers, printed commercial calendars and others.</p>
<p>- Launched Good Deal brand for school and office printed products.</p>
<p>- Broke Ground on The Paper Tree inSta. Ana Avenueas the future site</p>
<h2></h2>
<h2>2008</h2>
<p><a href="http://thepapertreeacademy.files.wordpress.com/2012/01/1-facade.jpg"><img class="size-full wp-image-780 aligncenter" title="1 Facade" src="http://thepapertreeacademy.files.wordpress.com/2012/01/1-facade.jpg?w=500" alt=""   /></a></p>
<p>- Completed the new office building and main warehouse.  Named it The Paper Tree Building in Sta. Ana.  Project successfully completed by Engineer Ron Agcopra.</p>
<p>- Transferred from the oldAlvarez Streetoffice to the newSta. Ana Avenue office.  In essence, transferred from one end ofSta. Ana Avenue to the other end.  Near now to Gaisano Mall.</p>
<p>- Opened Media Lab in the 3rd quarter of the year.  Media Lab is the offshoot of the marketing department of DUC.  It is tasked to produce art and marketing materials for DUC and outside clients.</p>
<p>- Opened Pronto Mario Quick Serve Cafe to serve customers coming into The Paper Tree store in Sta. Ana.</p>
<p>- Launched first catalogue-style website of The Paper Tree (www.thepapertree.com.ph)</p>
<h2></h2>
<h2>2009</h2>
<p><a href="http://thepapertreeacademy.files.wordpress.com/2012/01/2-hp.jpg"><img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-781" title="2 HP" src="http://thepapertreeacademy.files.wordpress.com/2012/01/2-hp.jpg?w=500" alt=""   /></a></p>
<p>- Got distributorship for HP papers.</p>
<p>- Released &#8220;Hi&#8221; brand of paper products into the market.</p>
<p>- Launched first fully operational SOS online store inMindanao.</p>
<p>- Launched Supplier Relationship Management (SRM) website built into the main website to automatically publish POs from the company, automatically email to inform and follow-up POs with vendors.</p>
<p>- Launched laptop-based Sales Force Automation (SFA) system for sales reps so that they can bring with them their laptops and work anywhere and transmit Sales Orders (SO) via internet.  In short, they can work from anywhere and still be like working inside the office.</p>
<h2></h2>
<h2>2010</h2>
<p>- Opened film-based adhesive tape slitting factory to cut costs on this product line.</p>
<p>- Closed DUC Retail Store in Sta. Ana cornerAlvarez Street.  Consolidated DUC Retail Store operations to the new main store at The Paper Tree Building inSta. Ana Avenue.</p>
<p><a href="http://thepapertreeacademy.files.wordpress.com/2012/01/3-sta-ana-wholesale.jpg"><img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-782" title="3 Sta. Ana Wholesale" src="http://thepapertreeacademy.files.wordpress.com/2012/01/3-sta-ana-wholesale.jpg?w=500" alt=""   /></a></p>
<p>- Initiated CCTV project for enhanced personnel and company security.</p>
<p>- Automated scheduling of picking lists at the warehouse.  Expert System in the warehouse module optimized picking times according to priority of delivery, and not on a first-come-first-served basis.</p>
<p>- Added a Training Room to The Paper Tree inBoltonbuilding.</p>
<p>- Added an IT Room to The Paper Tree inBoltonbuilding.</p>
<h2></h2>
<h2>2011</h2>
<p>- Started development on PhilHR as main initiative of IT Department.</p>
<p>- Converted Pronto Mario Quick Serve Cafe into a Pronto Mart Convenience Store.</p>
<p><a href="http://thepapertreeacademy.files.wordpress.com/2012/01/5-pronto.jpg"><img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-784" title="5 Pronto" src="http://thepapertreeacademy.files.wordpress.com/2012/01/5-pronto.jpg?w=500" alt=""   /></a></p>
<p>- Offered In-Store Meals at Pronto Mart.</p>
<p>- Offered EC Pay Bills Payment and Prepaid Load sales at Pronto Mart.</p>
<p>- Upgraded DUC ERP system to Computerized-Accounting System accredited by the BIR.  Now, all invoices are printed automatically without human intervention.</p>
<p>- Got Copyright and Patent for &#8220;CACHE&#8221; brand for School and Office Products.</p>
<p>- Launched &#8220;CACHE&#8221; White Glue as initial product carrying this brand.</p>
<p>- Started production for thermal paper roll slitting for use in metered Taxi receipts.</p>
<p>- Launched SMS Alerts System.  An automated SMS service to inform customers of status of transactions and billings from DUC ERP Transactions at the main office in Sta. Ana.</p>
<p>- Launched Customer Relationship Module (CRM) with Automated Incentive Module to help manage the growing sales force of DUC Wholesale Sales Teams and The Paper Tree Corporate Sales Teams.</p>
<h2></h2>
<h2>2012</h2>
<p>- Launched online CRM for Sales Reps</p>
<p>- Added Printing Press Sales Division</p>
<p>- Initiated an Online Resource Center (thepapertreeacademy.wordpress.com) for the DUC.</p>
<p>- Much More to Come!</p>
